286	     * owners are hard duplicates only when their WHOLE identityKey matches, so two members of the
287	     * same household (same lastName and postcode) with different telephones have different keys and
288	     * are both allowed — the later one is flagged a soft match instead. Telephone and email are
289	     * already stored normalized (E.164 / lower-cased); the lastName contributes only through its
290	     * {@link Soundex} code so it tolerates spelling variation.
291	     */
292	    public String getIdentityKey() {
293	        String tel = this.telephone == null ? "" : this.telephone;
294	        String mail = this.email == null ? "" : this.email;
